SUMMARY:Prague Metabolism and Signaling Symposium 2026
LOCATION:National Library of Technology (NTK)\, Campus Dejvice\, Prague\, C
 zech Republic
DESCRIPTION:Meeting bringing together experts at the intersection of metabo
 lism and signal transduction. ~30 invited speakers plus two keynotes\, wit
 h short talks and poster sessions. Chaired by David Sabatini (IOCB Prague/
 Boston) and Katerina Rohlenova. A dedicated closing 'mTOR Biology' session
  features Brendan Manning\, Kuang Shen\, Mario Pende and David Sabatini\, 
 with Michael N. Hall (the discoverer of TOR) giving the second keynote.\n\
 nWhy it matters for mTOR (★★★): Highest relevance in the calendar. C
 o-chaired by David Sabatini\, keynote by Michael N. Hall (discovered TOR)\
 , and an explicit 'mTOR Biology' session. Many speakers are core mTOR/meta
 bolism labs\, several of whom are authors in the Atlas corpus.\n\nSpeakers
  or organisers with a profile in the Atlas: David M. Sabatini\, Michael N.
  Hall\, Liron Bar-Peled\, Alejo Efeyan\, Gerta Hoxhaj\, Nada Y. Kalaany\, 
 Brendan D. Manning\, Reuben J. Shaw\, Kuang Shen\, Issam Ben-Sahra\, Anne 
 Brunet\, Luca Scorrano\, Mario Pende\n\nConference site: https://praguemet
 abolismsymposium.com/\n\nIn Oliver's mTOR Atlas: https://mtor-atlas.org/ev
 ents/#ev-prague-metabolism-and-signaling-symposium-2026
